      "created_at": "2016-07-29T09:08:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>As someone who isn't a playtester, can I make an observation about FV Tachyon and Spite?</p><p>FV Tachyon's power is \"Deal 1 target 1 Melee damage; you may move a burst card from your trash to the bottom of your deck, if you do use this power again now\". I'm assuming that PL626 would hit each time you cycle through the power causing you to take damage and discard the top 5 cards. As the card says use this power again now, each cycle through is a new power usage right?</p><p>If so, wait until PL626 comes out hit him with Hypersonic Assault (or a damage dealing burst then Hypersonic Assault if PL602 is in play) then use the Power phase to loop Tachyon's Power to one-shot Spite one damage at a time. You won’t run out of burst cards (unless you are really unlucky) as you’ll be putting 5 cards into your trash for every one you are putting back into your deck.</p><p>Wow, just wow!</p><p>Even if the retaliation only happens once. Just get Tachyon’s deck to below 5 then cycle in fodder to 5 then Fleet of Foot, Fleet of Foot, Fleet of Foot, Quick Insight, 3 more bursts for between 7 and 12 pings per turn without even taking into account any damage boosts. Oh, and every other hero draws 3 extra cards per turn.</p><p>For any other villain it is only going to be 7, and you can only get that engine going once your deck is empty which is harder to do, but against Spite I don't want to say game breaker, but...</p><p>Please say I’ve missed something.</p>",
