    {
      "id": 179606,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-07-29T14:22:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"emcg575797\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/emcg575797/48/2440_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> emcg575797:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I knew I was missing something! I think I got overly excited.I still think that comboing the three Fleets of Foot and Quick Insight would work. It would be useless against DR, but the idea of The Scholar, or Haka getting three extra cards per turn late game fills me with glee.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That works, just the opposite way, and obviously requires an empty deck and a second card play.</p>\n<p>Play quick insight, draw three cards, discard 2. &nbsp;Play 3 fleet of foot's, drawing the 2 cards you discarded and one more. &nbsp;With 4 cards in the trash you draw a card, leaving you with no trash and a deck of three cards.</p>\n<p>Or with Pushing the limits and HUD goggles:</p>\n<p>Play three fleet of foot and 1 more card. &nbsp;Play quick insight. &nbsp;Play three fleet of foot and nimble strike. &nbsp;you now have four in your deck/trash. &nbsp;Draw 2, one of them is guaranteed to be fleet of foot.</p>\n<p>We actually pulled this off with TLT and some other shenanigans. &nbsp;6 cards a turn drawn was crazy.</p>\n<p>EDIT: &nbsp;Fixed you naughty people.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:04:00.943Z",
